kins outraised pace lags badly and lacks outside support"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point firmly to Haridopolos: an R+8 seat, a large cash advantage, ratings consensus at Safe R, and markets giving Jenkins little chance. The only available polls, both from July and partisan-sponsored, still show him ahead by about nine, so a Likely R rating with a double-digit Republican margin fits the evidence.", "watch": "Any fresh independent polling in October showing Jenkins closing within single digits, or a surge of Democratic outside spending, would warrant moving this toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 74 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Haridopolos (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Mike Haridopolos seeks re-election in a Space Coast district that leans Republican by eight points, facing Democrat Jennifer Jenkins, a former Brevard County school board member. Haridopolos holds a clear financial edge, with about $1.2 million on hand to Jenkins' $108,000, and has secured the U.S. Chamber endorsement plus headlines touting federal housing money for Brevard County.\n\nThe ratings consensus is strongly Republican: most outlets call the race Safe R, with a few at Likely R. The two July polls, one Republican-sponsored and one Democratic-sponsored, both showed Haridopolos ahead by roughly nine points, though they are dated. Prediction markets give Jenkins only about a six percent chance. The race has drawn debates and local coverage of affordability and insurance issues, but no evidence yet of a genuine toss-up dynamic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0724, "margin": -8.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0928, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0611, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09